{"term":"blight","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:566b82cfc529e10fb2","definition":"A diseased condition suffered by a plant; specifically, a complete and rapid chlorosis, browning, then death of plant tissues such as floral organs, leaves, branches, or twigs, especially one caused by a fungus; a mildew, a rust, a smut.","example":"Proceed, inhuman Parent in thy Scorn; / Root up my Trees, vvith Blites deſtroy my Corn; / My Vineyards Ruin, and my Sheepfolds burn.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1b18daf8c2fffb98cc","definition":"The cause of such a condition, often unseen but believed to be airborne; specifically, a bacterium, a virus, or (especially) a fungus; also, an aphid which attacks fruit trees.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:315525c529ecbceccd","definition":"A state of cloudy, humid weather.","example":"And the youth stood by thy side and whispered to thee; and from his lips there came a reeking smoke, and in that smoke as in a blight the wings withered up.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:decf115c0aed56d9d2","definition":"A diseased condition of the face or skin; specifically, bleeding under the conjunctiva of the eye, a form of skin rash, or a palsy of the face due to cold.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, dated","register":"broadly, countable, dated, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b4a819612721aa92d6","definition":"Something that impedes development or growth, or spoils any other aspect of life.","example":"But a blight had come over my existence, and I only visited these people for the sake of the information they might give me on the subject in which my interest was so terribly profound.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bane"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:701e43f073709f8d86","definition":"A rundown and unsightly condition of an urban area; also, such an area.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, specifically","register":"countable, figuratively, specifically, uncountable","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c8976ed910dfa98422","definition":"To affect the fertility or growth of (a plant) with a blight (noun sense 1.1), especially one caused by a fungus; to blast, to mildew, to smut.","example":"But if it happens, as ſometimes it does, that this Vapour bears up along vvith it any noxious mineral Steams, it then blasts Vegetables, eſpecially thoſe vvhich are more young and tender: blights Corn and Fruits: and is ſometimes injurious even to Men vvho chance to be then abroad in the Fields.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["blighten"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight","blighted","blighter","blighting","blightingly","unblight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:584c5d007d4304525f","definition":"To affect (a body part) with a disease.","example":"[B]lighted be the tongue / That names thy name without the honour due!","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, dated","register":"broadly, dated, transitive","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight","blighted","blighter","blighting","blightingly","unblight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b594af28eaaa557f17","definition":"To impede the development or growth of (an aspect of life); to damage, to ruin, to spoil.","example":"Those obscene tattoos are going to blight your job prospects.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ball up","blight","bumble","botch","bugger up","bungle","contaminate","corrupt","crab","deprave","disrupt","disturb","foil","fuck up","jack up","mar","mess up","mishandle","mommick","pollute","put a crimp in","queer","ruin","screw up","soil","sour","spoil","stain","undo","upset","turn upside down","upset the applecart","vitiate","blighten"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight canker","blighten","blight in the eye","blightscape","blighty","eye blight","frictional blight","functional blight","Irish blight","planning blight","urban blight","blighted","blighter","blighting","blightingly","unblight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5da00938c251ca91b8","definition":"Of a plant: to suffer blight (noun sense 1.1).","example":"This vine never blights.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["blight-beetle","blight bird","blight ca